 @joemarais7683  Yep, it's produces slightly more input lag than when using just DLSS2 or DLSS2 with Reflex. However, any version of DLSS actually lowers input lag and with Reflex turned on, even more so. With DLLS3 and frame interpolation turned on, it still is producing less lag than playing native res with DLSS off, DLSS off with Reflex on, or with FSR 2 on or TAA on.
How the hell people can even complain about that, when it still is reducing lag over any those other 4 commonly used options is simply beyond me?
People play games with DLSS & Reflex turned off frequently and many titles still don't even support them. However, absolutely nobody does or ever did complain about the large amount input lag that native resolution puts out. It's actually one off the worst available options to choose, for putting the most amount of input lag.

